<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>HLA-HD Report &#8212; {{ sample }}</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; max-width: 900px; margin: 40px auto; color: #222; }
  h1 { color: #2c3e50; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 8px 12px; text-align: left; }
  th { background: #f0f4f8; }
  tr:nth-child(even) { background: #f9f9f9; }
  .badge { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 12px; font-size: 0.78em; font-weight: bold; margin: 2px; }
  .badge-yellow { background: #fff3cd; color: #856404; border: 1px solid #ffc107; }
  .badge-orange { background: #ffe5cc; color: #7d3c00; border: 1px solid #ff8800; }
  .badge-red    { background: #f8d7da; color: #842029; border: 1px solid #f5c2c7; }
  .badge-darkred { background: #842029; color: #fff; border: 1px solid #842029; }
  .badge-green  { background: #d1e7dd; color: #0f5132; border: 1px solid #a3cfbb; }
  .badge-grey   { background: #e9ecef; color: #495057; border: 1px solid #ced4da; }
  details { margin: 8px 0; }
  summary { cursor: pointer; font-weight: bold; }
  .note-box { background: #eef2ff; border-left: 4px solid #4a6cf7; padding: 12px; margin: 16px 0; }
  .evidence { margin: 18px 0 28px; padding: 14px; border: 1px solid #e3e3e3; border-radius: 8px; background: #fcfcfd; }
  .evidence img { max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin: 6px 0; }
  .cap { font-size: 0.85em; color: #555; margin: 4px 0 0; }
  .igv-btn { font-size: 0.72em; font-weight: normal; background: #4a6cf7; color: #fff; padding: 3px 9px; border-radius: 5px; text-decoration: none; margin-left: 8px; vertical-align: middle; }
  @media print {
    .igv-btn { display: none; }
    .evidence { page-break-inside: avoid; }
    a[href]:after { content: ""; }
  }
  footer { margin-top: 40px; font-size: 0.85em; color: #666; border-top: 1px solid #eee; padding-top: 12px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<h1>HLA Class I Report</h1>
<p><strong>Sample:</strong> {{ sample }}&emsp;
   <strong>Date:</strong> {{ run_date }}&emsp;
   <strong>HLA-HD:</strong> {{ hlahd_version }}</p>

<h2>HLA Class I Summary</h2>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Locus</th>
      <th>Two-field result</th>
      <th>Allele 1</th><th>P-group 1</th>
      <th>Allele 2</th><th>P-group 2</th>
      <th>Exon 2 cov</th><th>Exon 3 cov</th>
      <th>Call status</th>
      <th>Flags</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for locus in loci %}
    <tr>
      <td><strong>HLA-{{ locus.locus }}</strong></td>
      <td>{{ locus.two_field_genotype }}</td>
      <td>{{ locus.allele1 or 'Not typed' }}</td>
      <td>{{ locus.p_group1 }}</td>
      <td>{{ locus.allele2 or 'Not typed' }}</td>
      <td>{{ locus.p_group2 }}</td>
      <td>{{ locus.exon2_cov }}</td>
      <td>{{ locus.exon3_cov }}</td>
      <td>
        {% for s in locus.call_status %}
          <span class="badge {{ status_class.get(s, 'badge-yellow') }}">{{ s }}</span>
        {% endfor %}
      </td>
      <td>
        {% for f in locus.flags %}
          <span class="badge {{ flag_class.get(f, 'badge-yellow') }}">{{ f }}</span>
        {% endfor %}
      </td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

{% set detailed = [] %}
{% for locus in loci if locus.flags or locus.frequency_resolution_details or locus.est_mismatch
   or locus.phase_check in ['not_evaluated', 'incomplete'] %}{% set _ = detailed.append(locus) %}{% endfor %}
{% if detailed %}
<h2>Details</h2>
{% for locus in detailed %}
  <details open>
    <summary>HLA-{{ locus.locus }} &#8212; {{ locus.call_status | join(', ') }}{% for f in locus.flags %} [{{ f }}]{% endfor %}</summary>
    {% if locus.frequency_resolution_details %}
      <p><strong>Frequency resolution details</strong> (equally supported by the reads):
         {{ locus.frequency_resolution_details }}</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if locus.ambiguous_alleles and ('Phase ambiguity' in locus.flags or 'Shared P-group' in locus.flags) %}
      <p><strong>Equally supported pair(s) not in HLA-HD's final result:</strong> {{ locus.ambiguous_alleles }}</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if locus.phase_check in ['not_evaluated', 'incomplete'] %}
      <p><strong>Phase ambiguity check:</strong> {{ locus.phase_check | replace('_', ' ') }}
         (no IMGT alignment given, or an allele was missing from it).</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if 'Low exon depth' in locus.flags or 'Incomplete exon coverage' in locus.flags %}
      <p><strong>Coverage (mean depth, incomplete positions):</strong></p>
      <ul>
        {% for line in locus.coverage_detail %}
          <li>{{ line }}</li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    {% endif %}
    {% if locus.est_mismatch %}
      <p><strong>Internal check &#8212; est.txt mismatch:</strong> <code>{{ locus.est_mismatch_detail }}</code></p>
    {% endif %}
  </details>
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

<div class="note-box">
  <strong>Call status:</strong><br>
  <strong>Unique:</strong> A single genotype assignment remained after normalization to the reported (two-field) resolution.<br>
  <strong>Frequency-resolved:</strong> Multiple genotype assignments were equally supported by the sequencing reads. HLA-HD selected the reported genotype using its population-frequency ranking; the alternative assignment(s) remain compatible with the sequencing evidence.<br>
  <strong>Multiple best pairs:</strong> Multiple genotype assignments remained equally supported after population-frequency ranking. All remaining best-pair assignments are reported.<br>
  <strong>QC review:</strong> HLA-HD generated a reportable genotype, but one or more coverage metrics meet the criteria for additional review. May be reported together with Unique, Frequency-resolved or Multiple best pairs.<br>
  <strong>Failed:</strong> HLA-HD reported Not typed for the locus. No allele or P-group result is reported.<br>
  <br>
  <strong>Flags:</strong><br>
  <strong>Phase ambiguity:</strong> Competing genotype assignments differ only in haplotype phase and are equally supported by the sequencing reads.<br>
  <strong>Shared P-group:</strong> Competing two-field genotype assignments map to the same P-group and therefore encode identical peptide-binding domain amino acid sequences.<br>
  <strong>Frequency tie:</strong> Population-frequency ranking did not distinguish between the remaining read-supported genotype assignments; all remaining best-pair assignments are reported.<br>
  <strong>Low exon depth:</strong> HLA-HD mean coverage for exon 2 or exon 3 is below {{ min_exon_depth | int }}&times; for either allele.<br>
  <strong>Incomplete exon coverage:</strong> HLA-HD identifies one or more positions without coverage in exon 2 or exon 3 for either allele. A "(!)" marks the affected allele.
</div>

{% if pileup %}
<h2>Read Evidence at Discriminating / Mismatch Positions</h2>
<p>Stacked read counts (A/C/G/T) at the positions that distinguish the called alleles.
   Hatched (top) = allele&nbsp;1's expected base; dotted = allele&nbsp;2's; solid = any other base;
   red columns are low coverage. At est-mismatch / alternative-pair positions the dotted segment
   shows the alternative allele's expected base rather than allele&nbsp;2's.</p>
{% for locus in ['A', 'B', 'C'] if locus in pileup %}
  <div class="evidence">
    <h3>HLA-{{ locus }}
      <a class="igv-btn" href="{{ pileup[locus].igv_url }}">Open in IGV</a></h3>
    <img src="data:image/png;base64,{{ pileup[locus].chart_png }}" alt="HLA-{{ locus }} read pileup">
    <p class="cap">{{ pileup[locus].caption }}</p>
  </div>
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

<footer>
  HLA-HD {{ hlahd_version }} &bull; P-group reference: {{ pgroup_file }}
</footer>
</body>
</html>
